# FrontDesk AI release baseline
#
# Version:     1.3.0.3
# Released:    22 November 2026 (baseline 1.0.0.0: 21 November 2026)
# Owner:       Sanjay Karwa, Smart AI for Business
# Live:        https://frontdesk-ai-xi-gray.vercel.app
# Staff:       https://frontdesk-ai-xi-gray.vercel.app/staff
# Docs:        https://github.com/karwasanjay007/frontdesk-ai-docs
#
# This file marks the first public baseline of the dental front-desk chat
# submitted for the Freedom With AI Batch 10 build project. Answers come
# from the clinic file; anything else becomes a staff ticket. The model
# key stays on the server.
#
# Version 1.1.0.0 adds, beside the baseline and without changing what it does:
# a reply and a ticket when a patient asks for a person, with a seventh quick
# reply; search, status filter, sort and opt-in urgent alerts on the staff
# page; a form for the clinic file that writes into the same JSON box; an
# optional assistant name and the clinic's own quick replies in the file.
#
# Version 1.2.0.0 (22 November 2026, evening) adds to the staff page: the queue
# at a glance, CSV export, ready-made replies, a filter by ticket type and a
# private staff note; and a booking reply that states the named day's hours.
#
# Version 1.3.0.0 (22 November 2026, late evening) adds ticket numbers, the
# patient's chat thread inside a ticket, feedback on a reply, and tickets shared
# across devices through a server store (a private key per browser, a desk code
# for staff).
#
# Version 1.3.0.1 (23 November 2026): every tap target on both pages is at least 44 px (it was 40 on
# chips, some buttons and the clinic form fields); the width test checks 44 on both pages.
#
# Version 1.3.0.2 (25 November 2026), after the project feedback: a question that mixes timings with prices
# ("What are your timings and prices?") is answered from the clinic file with both; the light and dark button
# says which theme is on; the skip link puts the cursor in the message box in every browser.
#
# Version 1.3.0.3 (25 November 2026, late evening): a staff reply or a patient question is sent to the shared
# ticket store even when its tab goes to the background straight after (it used to wait until the tab was
# looked at again).
#
# Version 1.3.1.0 (27 November 2026), added on top after a check against the course build approach; nothing removed:
# an emergency reply begins with the emergency number in every language; more emergencies, Hinglish rule-break and
# discount requests are caught; a service asked with a qualifier the clinic file does not hold (laser, ceramic) gets
# "not sure" and a ticket, never a neighbouring price; a parent asking to bring a child is answered from the file.
# The model step uses temperature 0, one attempt and an 8-second limit; its text is checked against the clinic file
# on the server as well as in the browser; the route has a request limit and never rewords a safety reply.
#
# Version 1.4.0.0 (27 November 2026), added on top; nothing removed: the shared store as the course guideline says
# (Postgres through @neondatabase/serverless, plain SQL, three tables: messages, tickets, clinic_data), tickets
# shared by default, a staff edit of the clinic file applies from the next answer on every device, messages
# stored; the brand palette, fonts and mark; a staff page link in the top bar; the clinic details pinned on the
# right on a wide screen; a health route that says which store is in use.
